sing $1$s windows. On the static KUL and USTC datasets, it improves causal decoding over fixed-rate post-hoc HMM baselines by $5.6\\%$ and $2.0\\%$, respectively, showing the superiority of learning AAD as attention state sequence over isolated-window classification.\nView a PDF of the paper titled End-to-End Markov State Sequence Learning for Auditory Attention Decoding, by Yushan Yashengjiang and 5 other authors</div><li><a href=\"/pdf/2607.18614\" aria-describedby=\"download-button-info\" accesskey=\"f\" class=\"abs-button download-pdf\">View PDF</a></li><li><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2607.18614v1\" class=\"abs-button\" id=\"latexml-download-link\">HTML (experimental)</a></li><li><a href=\"/src/2607.18614\" class=\"abs-button download-eprint\">TeX Source\n      <div class=\"abs-license\"><a href=\"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\" title=\"Rights to this article\">view license</a></div>\n         accesskey=\"p\" title=\"previous in cs.SD (accesskey p)\" rel=\"nofollow\">&lt;&nbsp;prev</a>\n         title=\"next in cs.SD (accesskey n)\"  rel=\"nofollow\">next&nbsp;&gt;</a>\n  </div><div class=\"abs-switch-cat\">\n    <div class=\"switch context-change\">\n        <div class='bib-modal-title'>\n  <div><h3>Bookmark</h3></div><a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small\" href=\"http://www.bibsonomy.org/BibtexHandler?requTask=upload&amp;url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.18614&amp;description=End-to-End Markov State Sequence Learning for Auditory Attention Decoding\"\n     title=\"Bookmark on BibSonomy\">\n  <a class=\"abs-button abs-button-grey abs-button-small\" href=\"https://reddit.com/submit?url=https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.18614&amp;title=End-to-End Markov State Sequence Learning for Auditory Attention Decoding\"\n     title=\"Bookmark on Reddit\">\n          <div class=\"column lab-switch\">\n            <label class=\"switch\">\n          <div class=\"column lab-switch\">\n            <label class=\"switch\">\n          <div class